<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rajmahal</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rajmahal is a town on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ganges-plain">Ganges</a> in the Sahibganj district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jharkhand">Jharkhand</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, at the gateway between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bihar">Bihar</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengal">Bengal</a>. In 1576 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughals</a> defeated the last Bengal sultan near it. Man Singh made it the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengal-subah">Mughal Bengal</a> in 1595, under the name Akbarnagar, and it remained so, with interruptions, until the capital moved to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dhaka">Dhaka</a> in the early seventeenth century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rajmahal.jpg" alt="Rajmahal" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Prashant mandal · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hills_of_rajmahal.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
